blingstranger","id":114190975,"node_id":"U_kgDOBs5qfw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/114190975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger","html_url":"https://github.com/ramblingstranger","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-22T23:37:36Z","updated_at":"2024-11-22T23:43:26Z","body":"> FYI your commit is under a different account than the PR\r\n\r\nThanks for pointing that out! Just fixed it","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2495100973/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"resolved"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2495106932","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99565#issuecomment-2495106932","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99565","id":2495106932,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6UuE90","user":{"login":"tetrapod00","id":145553014,"node_id":"U_kgDOCKz2dg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/145553014?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00","html_url":"https://github.com/tetrapod00","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-22T23:45:25Z","updated_at":"2024-11-22T23:45:25Z","body":"You may find it helpful to run pre-commit locally: https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/contributing/development/code_style_guidelines.html#pre-commit-hook","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2495106932/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2495170685","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99565#issuecomment-2495170685","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99565","id":2495170685,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6UuUh9","user":{"login":"lyuma","id":39946030,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5OTQ2MDMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39946030?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma","html_url":"https://github.com/lyuma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-23T01:02:48Z","updated_at":"2024-11-23T01:02:48Z","body":"> Set all the vertices to NaN/Inf\nI believe your code for this was not correct. You were doing `vec3(1.0/0.0)` but the problem is many compilers/optimizers (these are inside the driver itself) will optimize out certain statements containing values known at compile time to be NaN.\n\nI usually use sqrt(value not known at compile time but always negative). For example, `VERTEX = vec3(sqrt(-VIEW_MATRIX[3].w));`\nIf done right without triggering compiler optimizers, this approach has worked on all PC hardware I have tested as well as all android based VR devices (tested on Quest 1 and newer). I have not tested on other mobile chipsets so I will defer to clayjohn's expertise.\n> Set all vertices outside of the view frustum\nCan also do this, but it doesn't help if everything is degenerate anyway.\n> Set all the vertices to the same value so that the primitive collapses to a point\nThis is the correct/best answer if the material setting affects the whole mesh. No need to depend on undocumented behavior if you can achieve the same effect by making all triangles degenerate.\n\nPersonally, though, I would like to question the overall approach of doing this. Why are we submitting the draw call and then culling it in the vertex shader? It seems to me that this culling property makes more sense to be applied in RenderingServer similar to how layer_cull_mask currently works on visual instances.\n\nThe proposal indicates a desire to make the debug materials on a demo project easier to test, but I think there ought to be a better way to do this that doesn't involve swapping around layers on materials. It just doesn't feel like the right place to do this even if it is possible, given that it includes a performance cost that users might not expect. (You can write this code in a shader material if needed)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2495170685/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2499027806","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99565#issuecomment-2499027806","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99565","id":2499027806,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6U9CNe","user":{"login":"ramblingstranger","id":114190975,"node_id":"U_kgDOBs5qfw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/114190975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger","html_url":"https://github.com/ramblingstranger","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-25T21:03:17Z","updated_at":"2024-11-25T21:24:43Z","body":"@clayjohn @lyuma I looked into culling before the draw call, but it's well beyond me. If you all definitely want to approach it from that direction, i could make a new issue (or amend the current issue) asking for it to be implemented on all 3D materials, and then see if someone else comes along who wants to tackle it.\r\n\r\nIf you think the current solution could work with minor tweaks, I'd be happy to make any necessary changes, such as changing how it is culled in the vertex function. If so, let me know what the best solution for this is... seems like maybe it is setting the vertices outside of the view frustum, per clayjohn's suggestion above.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2499027806/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2499033759","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99565#issuecomment-2499033759","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99565","id":2499033759,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6U9Dqf","user":{"login":"ramblingstranger","id":114190975,"node_id":"U_kgDOBs5qfw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/114190975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger","html_url":"https://github.com/ramblingstranger","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-25T21:06:34Z","updated_at":"2024-11-25T21:23:14Z","body":"> The proposal indicates a desire to make the debug materials on a demo project easier to test, but I think there ought to be a better way to do this that doesn't involve swapping around layers on materials. It just doesn't feel like the right place to do this even if it is possible, given that it includes a performance cost that users might not expect. (You can write this code in a shader material if needed)\r\n\r\n@lyuma Regarding this, my original goal for this PR was to provide a way for users who don't know shaders to more easily use an example project i'm working on, which you can find [here](https://github.com/thompsop1sou/custom-screen-buffers). (I know this project isn't an optimal solution. I've just put it up as a possible workaround until the compositor is complete.)\r\n\r\nI also thought being able to render different materials on different layers might be helpful for other visual effects, such as thermal vision. Of course that's already possible in shaders, but I thought it could be helpful to make that more accessible.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2499033759/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3979216072","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99565#issuecomment-3979216072","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99565","id":3979216072,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7tLgTI","user":{"login":"ramblingstranger","id":114190975,"node_id":"U_kgDOBs5qfw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/114190975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger","html_url":"https://github.com/ramblingstranger","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-01T06:00:19Z","updated_at":"2026-03-01T06:00:19Z","body":"I picked this issue back up and looked into culling before the draw call, per clayjohn's comment. I think I figured it out and have opened a new pull request. Closing this PR in favor of the new one: <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116915>","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3979216072/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]